The eFootball scene lives in WhatsApp groups and spreadsheets. Neekora turns it into one place where players find their people, enter competitions and build a record they can share.

Organisers publish a tournament from a template, players join from a shared link, check in and play. Both players confirm each result or raise a dispute with evidence, and the bracket updates itself. The full journey runs end to end today on the competition engine, with the backend as the next milestone.
